# Trim stale documentation

Documentation work is **not add-only**. Whenever you create or edit Markdown (User/Admin guides, plugin operator docs, Michu reports, platform overviews, changelogs as needed), actively look for text that is **superseded, replaced, or no longer relevant** and **delete or shorten** it in the same task.

If agents only append, guides bloat and readers get contradictory instructions.

## Required behaviour

Before claiming a doc edit is done:

1. **Scan the sections you touched** (and nearby related sections) for stale names, steps, settings, entry points, billing claims, Coming Soon promises, and duplicate explanations of the same fact.
2. **Remove or shorten** material that the new or corrected facts replace. Prefer one clear current story over "also formerly…" piles unless a one-line formerly note helps reviewers.
3. **Update companions** the same way: if page A drops a feature, pages that still describe it as current need the same trim (see `platform-docs-consistency.mdc`).
4. **Say what you removed** when useful: Michu reports use **What we removed from our guides**; for human edits, the changelog "What changed" / "Why" should mention trims when they are material.

## Typical triggers

| Situation | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Feature, setting, UI path, or workflow was removed or renamed | Delete obsolete steps; use the new name; drop dead links |
| New guidance replaces old guidance on the same topic | Keep the new text; delete the old paragraph/section instead of stacking both |
| "Coming Soon" or roadmap text is now factually wrong | Update or remove it |
| Duplicate marketing / repeated policy with no extra Paragon value | Prefer one short Paragon-specific summary; delete the redundant copy when you are already in that section |
| Intentionally disabled / turned-off policy note | **Keep** the policy note (do not delete "not enabled" wording just because upstream still ships the feature elsewhere) |

## Relationship to other automations

| Actor | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Michu** | Must trim when **upstream Cursor docs** drop or replace product behaviour we still document (`michu/automation-prompt.md`, `upstream-doc-drift.mdc`) |
| **Trundle** | Internal hygiene (links, facts, inventory); not a substitute for product-stale trims during authoring |
| **Human / agent + ParaDOCS** | Same trim duty on every doc edit, including plugin and Technical Documentation operator docs |

## Out of scope

- Style-only or tone-only rewrites with no factual stale content.
- Deleting formal AI02 policy text solely for brevity.
- Editing the ADO `CursorAI` mirror for content that lives on GitLab `cursor-test`.
